§ `Tests: s 263`

#ASSERT `s 263(1) the provisions of this section have effect` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 263(1) the provisions of this section have effect` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 263(2): refuse if the court is satisfied that (a) a person acting under s 172 would not seek to continue; (b) a future act has been authorised; (c) a past act was authorised before or ratified since
#ASSERT `s 263(2) permission (or leave) must be refused` `s 263(2)(b) the act or omission is yet to occur` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 263(2) permission (or leave) must be refused` `s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 263(2) permission (or leave) must be refused` `s 263(2)(b) the act or omission is yet to occur` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 263(2) permission (or leave) must be refused` `s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 263(2) permission (or leave) must be refused` `s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 263(2) permission (or leave) must be refused` `s 263(2)(b) the act or omission is yet to occur` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 263(2) permission (or leave) must be refused` `s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 263(2) permission (or leave) must be refused` `s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 263(3): the matters to take into account in particular: (a), (b), (e), (f) always; (c) for a future act, (d) for a past act
#ASSERT elem "(c) whether the act or omission could be, and in the circumstances would be likely to be, authorised by the company before it occurs, or ratified by the company after it occurs" (`s 263(3) the matters the court must take into account in particular` `s 263(2)(b) the act or omission is yet to occur`)
#ASSERT elem "(d) whether the act or omission could be, and in the circumstances would be likely to be, ratified by the company" (`s 263(3) the matters the court must take into account in particular` `s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`)
#ASSERT elem "(a) whether the member is acting in good faith in seeking to continue the claim" (`s 263(3) the matters the court must take into account in particular` `s 263(2)(b) the act or omission is yet to occur`)
#ASSERT elem "(f) whether the act or omission gives rise to a cause of action that the member could pursue in his own right rather than on behalf of the company" (`s 263(3) the matters the court must take into account in particular` `s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`)
#ASSERT elem "(e) whether the company has decided not to pursue the claim" (`s 263(3) the matters the court must take into account in particular` `s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`)
#ASSERT NOT (elem "(d) whether the act or omission could be, and in the circumstances would be likely to be, ratified by the company" (`s 263(3) the matters the court must take into account in particular` `s 263(2)(b) the act or omission is yet to occur`))
#ASSERT NOT (elem "(c) whether the act or omission could be, and in the circumstances would be likely to be, authorised by the company before it occurs, or ratified by the company after it occurs" (`s 263(3) the matters the court must take into account in particular` `s 263(2)(c) the act or omission has already occurred`))
#ASSERT `s 263(4) the court must have particular regard to the evidence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 263(4) the court must have particular regard to the evidence` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

